// [dcl.init.ref]/5 with [over.ics.ref]/1: unlike a *const* reference
// (see const_reference_parameter_binding_to_a_literal_is_allowed.scpp),
// a *mutable* `T&` cannot bind to a prvalue -- there is no place a write
// through it could ever land.
//
// This case lived in tests/movetest_source until the rule was stated as
// [over.ics.ref]/1 rather than as a borrow-root shape list. It used to
// be rejected by movecheck, because resolve_borrow_source_root refused
// "an arbitrary expression" as a borrow source -- one sentence standing
// for four separate rules. Now `identity(int&)` is simply not viable, no
// overload matches, and the call is reported where every other
// unresolvable call in the language is reported: codegen. Moved here so
// the assertion is "the compiler rejects it" rather than "this
// particular pass rejects it". (That movecheck reports no unresolvable
// call at all is a separate, pre-existing gap; see the PR's
// new-defects list.)
int identity(int& r) {
    return r;
}
int main() {
    return identity(5);
}
